<title>USA: Ancor Communications Inc Q4 net loss.</title>
<headline>Ancor Communications Inc Q4 net loss.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended  Twelve Months Ended</p>
<p>			  December 31,	    December 31,</p>
<p>		    1996	  1995	    1996	    1995</p>
<p> Net Sales $1,321,218  $1,636,832    $6,694,098    $4,672,951</p>
<p>Cost of Sales</p>
<p>		1,165,268     823,886     4,001,651     2,532,622</p>
<p>Total operating</p>
<p>  expenses  2,574,573   1,526,660     8,142,321     5,327,043</p>
<p>Operating loss</p>
<p>	    (2,418,623)   (713,714)    (5,449,874)   (3,186,714)</p>
<p> Net Loss (2,390,807)   (731,660)    (5,289,684)   (3,268,915)</p>
<p>Net loss per</p>
<p>  common share (0.24)	 (0.09)	  (0.60)	  (0.44)</p>
<p>Weighted average</p>
<p>shares outstanding</p>
<p>	     10,316,873   8,105,319     9,351,060     7,449,182</p>
<p>NOTE: Q4 1996 results include $0.01 a share loss, and full year 1996 a $0.03 a share loss, from eight percent convertible preferred share premium.</p>
<p>Company said Q4 hurt by $660,000 product return credit.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
